Xstack is a great tool for stacking large number of low-counts X-ray spectra, especially when focusing on average spectral shapes. While we acknowledge a few limitations, they are beyond current scope and won't affect the core functionality of the code. That said, contributions are still welcome!

 Spectral shape and normalization cannot both be preserved without an assumption [...] + In this mode:
    - source/background PI are summed directly (integer counts preserved at output);
    - full response (`ARFRMF`) is stacked with `FLX` weighting;
    - stacked `EXPOSURE` is the summed exposure;
    - stacked src/bkg `AREASCAL`, `BACKSCAL`, `CORRSCAL` are written as means of inputs;
    - if `var(x/mean(x))` is large for any of these three scale keywords, a warning is written in the log file.
